<td>Optus</td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="">
<th>State</th>
<td>WA</td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="#E3E3F3">
<th>Electorate (2022)</th>
<td>O'Connor</td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="">
<th>Local Government Area</th>
<td>Albany, Cranbrook, Denmark, Jerramungup, Manjimup, Narrogin, Plantagenet, Ravensthorpe, West Arthur, Williams</td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="#E3E3F3">
<th>Upgrade Type</th>
<td>Transmission diversity for a cluster of sites</td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="">
<th>Description</th>
<td>Adding additional backhaul to promote greater transmission redundancy at 21 key sites in a cluster.
The cluster sites are located in Albany, Bremer Bay, Cranbrook, Darkan, Denmark, Gledhow, Hopetoun, Kendenup, King River, Mount Barker, Mount Clarence, Mount Melville, Munglinup, Narrogin, Orana, Shadforth, Spencer Park, Walmsley, Walpole, Williams and Willyung.</td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="#E3E3F3">
<th>Site Status</th>
<td>Complete</td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="">
<th>Date Complete</th>
<td>20220930</td>
</tr></table></center>]]></description>
